  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">for support of TJNA&#x2019;s executive transition, institutional strengthening, and sustainability plans</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tax Justice Network Africa (TJNA) is a growing regional network of 44 civil society organizations including think tanks; trade unions; feminists; and youth-led, faith-based, and community-based organizations spread across 25 African countries. TJNA advocates for pro-poor tax policies and strengthening tax systems to promote domestic resource mobilization by challenging harmful investment practices, improving international tax transparency, and restoring the sovereignty of natural resources back to African countries. This organizational effectiveness grant will support TJNA to ensure enhanced organizational sustainability and a successful leadership transition. (Strategy: International Women&#x2019;s Economic Empowerment).</narrative>
  </description>
